From: Chad Monroe <chad.monroe@adtran.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 13:51:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: udp: do not fraglist-GRO forwarded multicast

Forwarded/bridged multicast UDP (e.g. IPTV) reaches the GRO layer
with no matching socket, so udp_gro_receive() unconditionally sets
is_flist and fraglist-coalesces up to UDP_GRO_CNT_MAX datagrams into
one superframe. On egress the superframe is re-segmented and
re-burst, which de-paces a real-time stream and can drop or reorder
datagrams. The aggregation provides no benefit for forwarded
multicast and shows up as pixelated IPTV when rx-gro-list is on.

Skip GRO for multicast destinations in udp4_gro_receive() and
udp6_gro_receive(), where the L3 destination is available. This
also covers the NETIF_F_GRO_UDP_FWD path. Unicast forwarding, the
intended beneficiary of fraglist GRO, is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
--- a/net/ipv4/udp_offload.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/udp_offload.c
@@ -877,12 +877,20 @@ INDIRECT_CALLABLE_SCOPE
 struct sk_buff *udp4_gro_receive(struct list_head *head, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	struct udphdr *uh = udp_gro_udphdr(skb);
+	const struct iphdr *iph = skb_gro_network_header(skb);
 	struct sock *sk = NULL;
 	struct sk_buff *pp;
 
 	if (unlikely(!uh))
 		goto flush;
 
+	/* Multicast UDP (e.g. IPTV) is forwarded with no socket to gate GRO;
+	 * fraglist-coalescing a real-time stream and re-segmenting it on
+	 * egress de-paces and drops frames. Do not GRO multicast.
+	 */
+	if (ipv4_is_multicast(iph->daddr))
+		goto flush;
+
 	/* Don't bother verifying checksum if we're going to flush anyway. */
 	if (NAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->flush)
 		goto skip;
--- a/net/ipv6/udp_offload.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/udp_offload.c
@@ -136,12 +136,20 @@ INDIRECT_CALLABLE_SCOPE
 struct sk_buff *udp6_gro_receive(struct list_head *head, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	struct udphdr *uh = udp_gro_udphdr(skb);
+	const struct ipv6hdr *iph = skb_gro_network_header(skb);
 	struct sock *sk = NULL;
 	struct sk_buff *pp;
 
 	if (unlikely(!uh))
 		goto flush;
 
+	/* Multicast UDP (e.g. IPTV) is forwarded with no socket to gate GRO;
+	 * fraglist-coalescing a real-time stream and re-segmenting it on
+	 * egress de-paces and drops frames. Do not GRO multicast.
+	 */
+	if (ipv6_addr_is_multicast(&iph->daddr))
+		goto flush;
+
 	/* Don't bother verifying checksum if we're going to flush anyway. */
 	if (NAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->flush)
 		goto skip;
